.TH JOINTEST 1
.SH NAME
jointest \- regression test for join(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jointest
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Jointest
loads
.BR /p9/dis/join.dis 's
in-process test seam,
.BR runfiles(args,\ path1,\ path2) ,
and checks it against golden output for: the default matched format,
.B -a
unpairable-line handling in both its attached
.RB ( -a1 )
and separate-word
.RB ( "-a 1" )
forms,
.BR -e ,
duplicate-key cross products, unrecognised options being silently
ignored,
.BR -- ,
both
.B -o
forms (comma-list and legacy space-separated) including that a later
.B -o
replaces rather than concatenates with an earlier one,
.BR -1 / -2 ,
.BR -j / -j1 / -j2 ,
the
.B -t
separator, and default-separator collapsing.
.PP
Unlike every other
.B p9/cmd
test,
.I runfiles
takes two real file paths rather than two strings:
.IR join 's
own algorithm is seek-based (see
.IR join (1)
and
.BR join.b 's
header comment) and there is nothing to seek in an in-memory string, so
this test writes real temporary files
.RI ( /jointest1.txt ", " /jointest2.txt )
and reads real output back.
.PP
Also checks the three real bugs preserved from the original (see
.IR join (1)'s
BUGS): the multi-digit
.B -o
field-number bug
.RB ( "-o 1.10,2.2" ,
checked to insert a spurious extra column, not error, after an initial
guess that it would error turned out wrong against the real oracle);
that an out-of-range
.B -o
field
.RB ( "-o 1.0" ,
which segfaults the real
.I join )
falls back to the
.B -e
string rather than crashing; and that a truncated line (100 or more
fields) is reported as a failure only after whatever output had already
happened.
.PP
Every expected string here was checked against a real Plan 9
.I join
binary first (this tree's local
.B plan9port
checkout), not assumed from reading
.BR join.b .
An earlier draft of two expectations here (repeated
.B -o
concatenating, and one
.B -j
test's own input data) turned out to be wrong until checked this way
\(em both fixed to match the real binary, not the other way around.
.PP
Prints one line per failure to standard error, a final
.IR N " passed, " N " failed"
summary to standard output, and exits with a non-nil status if
anything failed.
.SH SOURCE
.B /p9/cmd/jointest.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR join (1)
.SH BUGS
Runs
.I join
in-process via its
.B runfiles
seam, which takes real file paths directly \(em so it does exercise
real seeking, unlike a string-based seam, but it still does not exercise
.IR join 's
own
.BR init ,
argument-count/usage validation, or the
.B -
(standard input) file argument, none of which
.B runfiles
goes through.
.PP
Does not check that output already emitted before a truncation failure
survives intact \(em there is no seam for reading
.IR join 's
output separately from whether it raised, since
.I join
prints the failure only after all matching output has already happened;
the test only checks that the failure occurs, not what came before it.
.PP
Does not exercise
.B join - -
(both files from standard input, neither seekable, a hard error in the
original) at all \(em real files are always seekable, so
.I runfiles
cannot construct that case.
